What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/blink
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	6.18
Contact:	linux-leds@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(WO) Start or stop blinking the LED with the default
		hardware pattern of 1 Hz.

		Writing a true value ("1", "y", "on") starts blinking at the
		current brightness, or at full brightness when the LED is
		off. Writing a false value ("0", "n", "off") turns the LED
		off. Any active trigger is removed first.

		The file exists for Android lights HALs that drive the
		notification LED by writing 0 or 1 here.
